                            <comment id="16714704" author="agoncharuk" created="Mon, 10 Dec 2018 13:19:43 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=sergey-chugunov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;sergey-chugunov&quot;&gt;sergey-chugunov&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=voropava&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;voropava&quot;&gt;voropava&lt;/a&gt;, I see that we we return an error code for other errors, but for some reason we throw an exception when max number of retries is exceeded. Is there any reason for that? As far as I understand, we will print a stacktrace in this case, which is not very nice. Would be better if we return a similar error code when the number of retries is exceeded.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
